WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.770
Weeding in the summer.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.720
I'm finally here!

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.620
I was trying to take a shortcut,

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.170
but the weeds were so 
thick that I got lost.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:57.130
Yes, I've heard other customers 
have gotten lost, too.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.910
I live next door,

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:01.390
but it took me twenty 
minutes to get here.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.070
These weeds are thick.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.060
Let's sit inside.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.250
Okay, let's do it!

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.070
What are you doing, Polar Bear?

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.730
I'm enjoying the cool breeze 
as I sit on the terrace drinking

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.290
an ice cold mint tea.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.040
That's not what I meant.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.220
Why am I weeding your café's lawn

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.010
while you're sitting 
there, drinking tea?!

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.370
I usually live where it's cold.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.810
So do I!

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.920
In what world is there a penguin

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.500
who weeds in the middle of summer?!

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.970
Thank you for the meal.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.770
I'll be seeing you.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.790
Mr. Llama, where are you going?

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:54.060
I can't eat anymore, 
so I figured I'd leave.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.380
Wait a minute.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.870
Why are you going home?

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.740
We just started weeding.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.570
But I'm full.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.660
But weeding is much more than that.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.490
Let's try a little harder.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.530
But... my stomach will burst.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.020
That's not what I meant...

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.920
Um... is there any way to weed
that doesn't involve eating?

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:20.910
Oh, I see.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.010
Let me think.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.020
Are you asleep?

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.870
I'm awake.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.190
You were totally asleep.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.490
Would you like some mint tea?

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.110
Oh, thank you.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.070
Come on, guys.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.780
Let's work harder!

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.950
I'd like to try harder,

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.920
but I can only eat eucalyptus.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.060
I'm saying...

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.540
there are other ways to weed
that don't involve eating.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.260
Mr. Penguin.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.540
I found a weird shaped rock.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.340
We didn't need to know that.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.090
Let's get rid of some weeds.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.550
Mr. Penguin.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.720
What is that, Miss Sasako?

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:09.890
It's a clay figure.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.280
I found it.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.520
I guess you didn't need to know that.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.860
What is with this yard?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.480
You often find them here.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.440
It's a spaceman clay figure.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.400
Yes.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.010
What a weird face.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:31.690
Am I the only one that's 
taking this seriously?

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:34.370
I am...

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.290
here too...

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.870
Sloth!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:48.880
I'll... do... my... best...

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.360
At least you're determined.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.190
The air conditioning is so cool.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:08.620
Hey, Mom, could you bring 
me some bamboo grass?

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:10.970
It's nice and cool, isn't it?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.610
Oh, Mr. Penguin, 
what are you doing here?

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:17.790
What do you mean what am I doing here?!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.830
What happened to weeding?!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.800
Why do you like weeding 
so much, Mr. Penguin?

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.090
I don't like it!

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.710
But at this rate, 
we won't finish today!

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.220
All right.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.060
Jeez.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.870
Then, let's go.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.690
Okay.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.740
I'll be there right after my nap.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.370
Don't suck me up!

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.420
It's so hot.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:55.320
It's hot for me, too.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.110
What's that?

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.660
A fire?

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.790
What?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.780
Let's hurry, Panda!

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.920
Okay.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.180
Hey, now.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.590
What are you doing?

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.350
Barbecuing.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:17.260
Didn't you say you were 
full, Mr. Llama?!

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.810
Barbecue goes into a separate stomach.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.420
I've never heard anything like that!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:26.680
Mr. Penguin, I found this 
clay figure over there.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:27.700
Again?

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:32.390
That's amazing and all, 
but we didn't need to know that.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.250
Let me see! Let me see!

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.170
It's ready, Mr. Llama.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.170
Here you go.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.240
Thank you very much.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:46.100
I'm going to collapse now.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.840
Mr. Penguin?!

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.560
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.030
Nice shot!

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:02.080
It's not that hard at all.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.510
What are you doing?!

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.020
Golfing.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:10.300
No one is following my example
of working hard.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.200
Sorry.

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:14.420
Mr. Penguin.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.660
What is it, Miss Sasako? 
Another clay figure?

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:21.620
No. We actually all got 
this section done.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:22.800
Huh?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.090
Oh.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.000
Mr. Llama said it would be cooler in the shade

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.050
and you'd be able to rest here.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.970
The sun was pretty strong 
on the terrace.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.300
Sorry about that.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:43.650
I thought it'd be a lot more fun 
if we did this all together.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.400
Because...

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:50.020
it's fun just having everyone together.

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:02.370
You're right.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:05.290
It seems I forgot something 
rather important.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.250
Would you like some mint tea?

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.210
Please.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.180
The rest of us should 
get back to weeding.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.140
Okay.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.040
Please take it easy, Mr. Penguin.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.730
Well, then.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.560
Let's give it another go.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.560
I can't eat anymore...

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.820
It's your turn, Mr. Penguin.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.780
It's... all... good...

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:44.370
I'll... do the...

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:48.290
This isn't ending.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.620
What should we do?

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:55.340
I ate too much barbecue and 
can't eat any more weeds.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.230
Hello?

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:08.080
What the hell do you want,

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.960
calling me over in this damn heat?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.240
The yard was getting overgrown with weeds.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.510
The weeds in the yard?

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.230
You aren't thinking about asking me

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.410
to pull the weeds, are you, Polar Bear?!

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.070
Could you?

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:24.540
Could I?

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.460
What do you mean, could I?!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.760
Is that good enough?!

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.690
Such violent, yet such careful work.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.910
Give me food!

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.150
Here.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.610
It's great!

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.800
See ya later!

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.510
And then he left like a storm.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.680
I'll treat you today.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:05.380
Huh?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.450
I've caused you a lot of 
trouble, Mr. Penguin.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:10.630
Let's have a drink.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:14.440
Okay!

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.010
We worked so hard today!

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.180
You should come over here and 
have a drink, too, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.680
This is fun!

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.150
Isn't it?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.200
In Preparations

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.580
What did you want to talk 
about, Polar Bear?

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.080
Well...

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.520
What's the matter?

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.850
I'll be happy to listen.

00:10:58.430 --> 00:10:59.550
What?!

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.990
It's only been a few days 
and they grew this much?!

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:06.520
The weeds grow fast in the summer.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:10.980
I'm not seeing why I should help here.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:14.320
You know, because I'm an animal 
that's from a cold place.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:16.480
I'm telling you, so am I!

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:18.770
This is a clay figure I just found.

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:22.020
Miss Sasako,

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.040
we really don't need
 to hear that anymore.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:30.910
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:29.890
Mr. Penguin's Romance.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.010
It's totally summer.

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:37.380
It is summer.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.510
You can hear the cicadas 
quite well this year.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.890
The males use their internal 
sound-producing organ

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.230
and sound-producing membrane 
to produce the sound,

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:47.680
then use their resonance 
chamber to amplify the sound

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:48.970
to call upon the females.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:54.180
Could you stop saying things 
with so little emotion?

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.280
What's wrong, Panda?

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.290
Don't you want a panda red bean bun?

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:02.450
Are you not feeling well?

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:05.510
Instead of bread everyday,

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:08.660
could you buy some 
fancy fruits once in a while?

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.890
But Miss Penko isn't at the fruit shop.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.400
Mr. Penguin.

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:15.580
What is it? Do you want some bread?

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.330
No, it's not that.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.940
Didn't you say that, come summer,
you'd confess your love to Miss Penko,

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.550
and take her for a drive?

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:28.960
It's already summer.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.250
I know I said summer,

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:36.310
but I didn't say it 
would be this summer.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.380
It could be next year,

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:40.320
or even the year after that.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.640
Or even ten years from now.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.990
Was this really supposed 
to take that much time?

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:49.100
Why don't you just go ask 
her out real quick—

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.360
What do you mean, real quick?!

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.540
Wait a minute!

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:55.510
I think it's a good idea.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.460
Why don't you go ask her out?

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.500
What?!

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:03.700
Well, I have to prepare my heart 
if I'm going to confess.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.430
Er, um... and before that,

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.660
I have to get ready to start
 to prepare my heart.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:11.350
But if you don't hurry and confess,

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.600
someone might beat you to it.

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:19.020
But what if I get rejected?

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:20.480
It'll be okay.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:23.720
You haven't been rejected yet.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:25.050
He's right!

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:28.410
First ask her out, 
and then get rejected.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.970
Mr. Polar Bear!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.330
You're right.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.460
I was thinking of some future summer,

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:39.960
but maybe I'll just ask her out.

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.150
That's the spirit!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.980
Yeah! If you're going to be rejected, 
you should get it over with.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:48.230
Panda!

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.640
All right! I'm going to do it!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.140
And then I'll finally 
know her name for sure.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:54.870
What?

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:56.500
What?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:57.850
It's not Miss Penko?

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.020
Huh? Didn't I tell you?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:04.020
"Miss Penko" is the name 
I gave her.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.410
You don't mean...

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.780
that you don't know her name?

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.630
I have no idea.

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:10.590
Is that bad?

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:11.390
But...

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:12.920
Then tell me, Miss Sasako,

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.850
haven't you ever thought that a flower

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:16.620
you didn't know the name of was pretty?

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.970
Haven't you ever eaten a 
delicious fish that you

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:20.200
didn't know the name of?

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:22.450
Haven't you ever been 
moved by a song you

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:23.700
didn't know the name of?

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:25.780
Haven't you ever thought the scenery

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:27.240
I get it, so please, just go.

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:27.630
of an unknown place was beautiful?

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:28.950
Bye!

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:34.840
He doesn't even know her name.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.040
I wonder if he'll be okay.

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:43.090
Thank you very much.

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:45.400
Welcome!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.930
U-Um...

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:51.030
I didn't come today to get 
 service coupons!

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:56.000
<i>I didn't have to mention that...</i>

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:03.920
<i>I'm going to wait... 
until everyone leaves.</i>

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:06.970
I'll come again.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.400
Thank you very much.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.480
<i>Now's my chance.</i>

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.710
<i>Now's my only chance.</i>

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:17.390
<i>But I'm getting nervous.</i>

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:19.550
<i>What am I supposed to 
do at times like these?</i>

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:23.040
Person

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.020
<i>I write "person" on my 
hand and swallow it.</i>

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.520
<i>Or, wait...</i>

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:27.530
<i>Since I'm a penguin,</i>

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:30.920
<i>am I supposed to write "penguin" 
three times and swallow it?</i>

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:31.910
Pe

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:36.160
Pe-n-gui-n, pe-n-gui-n, pe-n-gui-n.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:32.240
Pen

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:32.610
Pengui

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:32.990
Penguin

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:33.370
Penguin Pe

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:33.740
Penguin Pen

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.120
Penguin Pengui

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:34.490
Penguin Penguin

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:34.870
Penguin Penguin Pe

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:35.240
Penguin Penguin Pen

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:35.620
Penguin Penguin Pengui

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.620
Penguin Penguin Penguin

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.950
How the heck am I supposed to 
swallow that many letters?!

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:40.660
Um...

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:44.030
I'm sorry for being so loud!

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:47.170
No, thank you for coming 
by all the time.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:51.620
I-It's no big deal.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:54.800
I can tell that you're in love...

00:15:58.390 --> 00:15:59.380
with the bread.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.150
Thank you very much!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.150
Um...

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:08.570
Yes?

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:12.600
I've always liked you!

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.460
Please go on a date with me!

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:16.850
I'll be waiting in front of the 
station on Sunday at 1 PM!

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:17.620
Huh?

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:18.960
'Kay, bye!

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:26.540
Apparently, Mr. Penguin

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:31.200
has been asking her out 
every day since then.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.930
Today's the fourth day in a row.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.930
Apparently he's going to keep 
trying until he gets a yes.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.100
Isn't that a little pushy?

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:39.260
I don't think so.

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:42.420
Mr. Penguin's trying his best!

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:44.680
How would you feel

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:48.070
if someone asked you out 
persistently every day, Miss Sasako?

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.020
Huh?

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.030
Well, I wouldn't like that...

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:41.580
It's been a week today.

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:44.650
It must feel nice, to have someone

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:47.120
feel so strongly about just you.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.290
Really?

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:49.920
Of course!

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:53.160
How would you feel if someone

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:56.840
persistently asked you out every day 
for a week, Miss Sasako?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.270
Well, I wouldn't like that...

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:14.280
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:17.870
I've always liked you!

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:19.540
Please go on a date with me!

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:22.600
I'll be waiting in front of the 
station on Sunday at 1 PM!

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:26.160
Tomorrow is Sunday, right?

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:30.260
Uh, yes! I'm sorry, it's rather sudden.

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:32.380
Okay.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.290
Huh?

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:45.020
I think that we both loved 
each other from the start.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:49.980
I went to the bakery every day for week
and kept asking her out.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.210
I see...

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:54.380
And then on the last day of that week...

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:56.680
That's when Penmi...

00:18:56.680 --> 00:19:01.530
Oh, her name is Penmi, 
not Penko.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.950
You should totally ask 
me what Penmi did next.

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:07.050
This is the fifth time.

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:09.420
Should we really ask again?

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:13.920
Ask me what Penmi did next.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.950
So what did Penmi do?

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:20.660
She asked, "Tomorrow is Sunday, right?"

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:22.390
We got it.

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:26.200
It was fate for us to fall 
in love with each other.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.480
Oh, have some bread.

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.350
No need to hold back, dig in!

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:30.810
Well, then,

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.770
see you again tomorrow!

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:38.660
I wonder how many times we'll 
have to ask him tomorrow.

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:41.230
Probably around twenty.

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:53.560
I wonder if Penmi is here yet.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.020
Maybe I was a little early.

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.510
Penmi!

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:06.140
Hey, Penmi!

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.190
What? My name is Penko.

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:10.290
Huh?

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:12.210
What's going on?

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:15.140
What?! Another Penmi?!

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.650
What are you talking about?

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:18.570
My name is Penka!

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:19.750
Huh?!

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:24.080
Hey, I thought you said you loved me!

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.990
What the?! Are you Penmi?

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.160
I'm Penna!

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:29.660
I'm Penno!

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:31.670
What's the meaning of this?

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.930
Y-You've got it all wrong, Penmi!

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:34.960
I'm Penjolina.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.800
Penjolina?

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.890
Hey, Mr. Penguin.

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:42.290
I'm sorry, Penmi. This is...

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:43.030
I'm Penuelle.

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:44.060
Penuelle?!

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:45.640
Mr. Penguin.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:46.660
Yes?!

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:48.230
I'm Penmi.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.930
What's the meaning of this?

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:55.350
Um... I'm not sure myself.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:21:00.140
What's the meaning of this?!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.230
P-Penmi!

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:03.950
Penno! Stop!

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.150
Penmi! Penmi! Help!

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:17.210
I never would have thought 
there were seven of them.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:20.170
I had no idea I was asking out 
someone different each day.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.050
It's because of the 
shifts at the bakery.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:24.300
Penko

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:25.430
Penna

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:26.180
Penuelle

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:26.590
Penjolina

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:27.160
Penno

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:27.550
Penka

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:29.300
Penmi

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:31.560
nmi

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:31.260
Curse those shifts.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:34.600
I'm leaving.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.080
Already?

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.890
I can feel their presence.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:42.500
See ya!

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:01.030
It's good that Mr. Penguin was 
finally able to confess.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:04.510
I wonder if this is how it 
should have ended up.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:07.010
How would you feel if you had to

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:11.470
listen to someone gush about 
their loved one every day?

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:16.740
Not sure.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:24.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.650
Next Time

00:23:57.970 --> 00:23:59.680
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin!

00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:00.780
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.780 --> 00:24:02.390
I feel rather uneasy.

00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:03.280
Really?

00:24:03.280 --> 00:24:06.450
I hope nothing bad happens 
to you, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:06.450 --> 00:24:07.540
This is reserved just for me?

00:24:07.540 --> 00:24:10.530
Could it be that you had some 
work done that's not minor?

00:24:10.530 --> 00:24:11.550
I have not.

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:13.210
However, I'm feeling a bit uneasy, too.

00:24:13.210 --> 00:24:14.890
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:16.710
Next week's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:18.670
will be fifty times bigger in size.

00:24:18.670 --> 00:24:21.030
What is? What's going 
to be fifty times bigger?

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:24.520
Mr. Grizzly Goes on an Adventure
A Strange Shop

00:24:21.030 --> 00:24:22.370
Miss Sasako, end it, please.

00:24:22.370 --> 00:24:23.520
Enjoy!
